    THE ARCHIVE DOES NOT REPRODUCE. Everything below is a different
    experiment from §53's and CANNOT be read against its null.

  G1 -- THE DECOMPOSITION'S IDENTITY, re-earned in the window this section
  reads. gap - (slot + resid) over every scored creature in e6-e7 on every
  arm. The count compared is printed and an EMPTY SET IS A FAILURE OF THE
  GATE, not a pass of the identity -- §58's clause 1 could have passed on
  zero cells and the smoke is what caught it
  (`vacuity-gate-cannot-guard-a-rejection`).
