    T1.ORACLE    identity 0.00e+00   worst |resid| 0.00e+00   over 0 creatures   (pinned: resid is identically 0 by arithmetic)
    worst identity 0.00e+00 over 0 creature-windows   *** FAIL -- EMPTY SET ***

  G2 -- VACUITY, ON THE ARM THAT IS KNOWN TO EXPRESS AND AT THE PRIMARY'S
  GRANULARITY. Can a two-eighth window carry a large slot term at all? A
  vacuity gate on the DERIVED arm cannot answer that, because its reading is
  the thing in question. Required: T1.ORACLE's FRESH e6-e7 >= its own FRESH
  whole-session value, both at this budget -- budget-relative on purpose,
  since an absolute 900k threshold is the `baseprobe-gate` defect §58 hit.
    T1.ORACLE fresh e6-e7   +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n 0)
    T1.ORACLE fresh e1-e8   +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n 0)
    window >= whole session   *** FAIL -- EMPTY OR SINGLETON SET ***

  G3 -- DISJOINTNESS. `seed + r * 7919` is injective in r, so the primary's
  reps cannot collide with the archive's. **THIS IS ARITHMETIC AND NOT A
  GATE** -- it cannot fail for a measured reason, so it is printed as a
  derivation and claims nothing (`open-is-unfalsifiable-on-an-instrument`).
    ARCHIVE r 0..35    seeds 00000000013527c9 .. 0000000001396276
    PRIMARY r 36..79   seeds 0000000001398165 .. 00000000013eb38a   gap 7919
    The primary's lowest seed exceeds the archive's highest by one stride
    of 7919, so the two sets share no creature.

